{{Politics of Romania}}

Presidential elections were held in [[Romania]] on 4 May 2025, with a second round on 18 May 2025. [[Nicușor Dan]] and [[George Simion]] were the two candidates who advanced to the second round, in which the former was victorious. [[Presidency of Nicușor Dan|Dan's term]] as the sixth [[president of Romania]] began on 26 May.

The election was scheduled in January 2025 following the annulment of the [[2024 Romanian presidential election]] citing [[Accusations of Russian interference in the 2024 Romanian presidential election|alleged Russian meddling]] in favour of first-round winner [[Călin Georgescu]]. The campaign was characterised by political instability and a series of [[2024–2025 Romanian election annulment protests|protests against the annulment]]. On 7 March, Georgescu was barred from running, pending several criminal investigations, with the [[Alliance for the Union of Romanians]] (AUR) leader Simion announcing his candidacy in Georgescu's place.

Simion, who won 40.96% of the vote in the first round, faced Dan, who garnered 20.99% of the vote, in the second round that was held on 18 May 2025.<ref>{{Cite web |date=4 May 2025 |title=Romanian election results: Trump fan George Simion wins first round, Nicușor Dan comes second |url=https://www.politico.eu/article/romanian-election-exit-polls-george-simoon-hard-right/ |access-date=8 May 2025 |website=POLITICO |language=en-GB}}</ref> Dan won with 53.6% against Simion's 46.4%. On 20 May, having previously conceded the election and congratulated Dan on his victory,<ref name=":6" /> Simion stated that he had formally filed a contest of the results with the [[Romanian Constitutional Court]], alleging mass voter fraud.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://apnews.com/article/romania-election-annulment-europe-simion-hardright-09647fefa8198d2f845f654639f50feb | title=Hard-right candidate who lost Romania's presidential race contests results at top court | website=[[Associated Press News]] | date=20 May 2025 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/20/defeated-romanian-ultranationalist-says-he-will-ask-court-to-annul-presidential-election | title=Defeated Romanian ultranationalist 'will ask court to annul election' | work=The Guardian | last1=Henley | first1=Jon | date=20 May 2025 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.politico.eu/article/romania-election-loser-far-right-george-simion-challenges-results-court/ | title=Romanian vote loser Simion claims France interfered in election | date=20 May 2025 }}</ref> Simion's request for the annulment of the election was rejected by the Court two days later, and [[Presidency of Nicușor Dan|Dan's presidency]] began on 26 May.<ref name=":4" /><ref>{{Cite news |last=Henley |first=Jon  |date=2025-05-18 |title=Centrist Nicuşor Dan defeats far-right rival in Romanian presidential election |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/18/centrist-nicusor-dan-on-course-to-beat-far-right-rival-in-romanian-election-exit-polls-suggest |access-date=2025-06-06 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref>

== Background ==

=== Previous election annulled ===
On 6 December 2024, the [[2024 Romanian presidential election]], was annulled by the [[Constitutional Court of Romania]], 48 hours before the second round was to be held, citing alleged Russian intervention on behalf of independent candidate, [[Călin Georgescu]], who took a shock lead in the first round with 23%.<ref>{{Cite web |date=6 December 2024 |title=Anulate, rezultatele primului tur al alegerilor prezidențiale din România |url=https://www.vaticannews.va/ro/mapamond/news/2024-12/prezidentiale-romania-anulat-balotajul-2024.html |access-date=29 December 2024 |website=Vatican News |language=ro |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241207235902/https://www.vaticannews.va/ro/mapamond/news/2024-12/prezidentiale-romania-anulat-balotajul-2024.html|archive-date=7 December 2024|url-status=live}}</ref> [[Supreme Council of National Defence (Romania)|CSAT]] said the campaign was "identical" to the online campaign launched by Russia before its [[Russian invasion of Ukraine|invasion of Ukraine]]. On 20 December, an investigation was published showing that [[National Liberal Party (Romania)|PNL]] had seemingly paid for one of the [[TikTok]] campaigns.<ref name=":1">{{Cite web|url=https://hotnews.ro/anaf-a-descoperit-ca-pnl-e-cel-care-a-platit-o-campanie-care-l-a-promovat-masiv-pe-calin-georgescu-pe-tiktok-snoop-este-campania-echilibru-si-verticalitate-despre-care-csat-a-spus-ca-este-identica-cu-1866501|title=INVESTIGAȚIE. ANAF a descoperit că PNL e cel care a plătit o campanie care l-a promovat masiv pe Călin Georgescu pe TikTok / SNOOP: Este campania "Echilibru și Verticalitate", despre care CSAT a spus că este "identică" cu campania online lansată de Rusia înainte de invadarea Ucrainei – HotNews.ro|date=20 December 2024|language=ro |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241220190747/https://hotnews.ro/anaf-a-descoperit-ca-pnl-e-cel-care-a-platit-o-campanie-care-l-a-promovat-masiv-pe-calin-georgescu-pe-tiktok-snoop-este-campania-echilibru-si-verticalitate-despre-care-csat-a-spus-ca-este-identica-cu-1866501|archive-date=20 December 2024|url-status=live}}</ref> PNL interim president [[Ilie Bolojan]] had stated that the campaign was altered illegally to favour Georgescu but did not blame the company they worked with for the alteration.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.g4media.ro/ilie-bolojan-despre-campania-pnl-deturnata-catre-calin-georgescu-pe-parcursul-campaniei-s-a-schimbat-adresa-aceasta-deturnare-nu-a-fost-facuta-de-firma-kensington-dovada-ca-a-facut-o-plange.html|title=Ilie Bolojan despre campania PNL deturnată către Călin Georgescu: "Pe parcursul campaniei s-a schimbat adresa. Această deturnare nu a fost făcută de firma Kensington dovadă că a făcut o plângere penală"|date=13 January 2025|website=G4Media.ro|language=ro|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250114224738/https://www.g4media.ro/ilie-bolojan-despre-campania-pnl-deturnata-catre-calin-georgescu-pe-parcursul-campaniei-s-a-schimbat-adresa-aceasta-deturnare-nu-a-fost-facuta-de-firma-kensington-dovada-ca-a-facut-o-plange.html|archive-date=14 January 2025|url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Second Ciolacu cabinet ===
After the [[2024 Romanian parliamentary election]], the [[second Ciolacu cabinet]] was formed as a minority coalition between [[Social Democratic Party (Romania)|PSD]], [[National Liberal Party (Romania)|PNL]], and [[Democratic Alliance of Hungarians in Romania|UDMR]], with confidence and supply from [[Romanian ethnic minority parties|minority parties]], on 23 December 2024. Furthermore, [[Ilie Bolojan]] became [[President of the Senate of Romania]] and [[Ciprian-Constantin Șerban]] became the [[President of the Chamber of Deputies of Romania]]. The cabinet passed with a seven-vote majority and became official. Opposition leaders (most prominently [[George Simion]] and [[Party of Young People|POT]] Leader [[Anamaria Gavrilă]]) called the cabinet illegitimate and for the resignation of incumbent president [[Klaus Iohannis]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=22 December 2024 |title=Cine vor fi miniștrii din noul Guvern și cum s-au împărțit portofoliile între PSD, PNL și UDMR. Emil Hurezeanu și Daniel David, printre viitorii miniștri |work=HotNews.ro |url=https://hotnews.ro/cum-isi-impart-psd-pnl-si-udmr-ministerele-in-noul-guvern-cea-mai-recenta-varianta-de-lucru-luata-in-calcul-de-liderii-coalitiei-1867401 |access-date=31 December 2024 |language=ro|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241222165605/https://hotnews.ro/cum-isi-impart-psd-pnl-si-udmr-ministerele-in-noul-guvern-cea-mai-recenta-varianta-de-lucru-luata-in-calcul-de-liderii-coalitiei-1867401|archive-date=22 December 2024|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=31 December 2024 |title=Cine sunt miniștrii din noul Guvern Ciolacu. Noul cabinet va avea 16 ministere |url=https://www.euronews.ro/articole/cine-sunt-ministrii-din-guvernul-ciolacu-coalitie-psd-pnl-udmr |access-date=31 December 2024 |website=Euronews |language=ro |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250221090405/https://www.euronews.ro/articole/cine-sunt-ministrii-din-guvernul-ciolacu-coalitie-psd-pnl-udmr |archive-date=21 February 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=27 December 2024 |title=Le Figaro: Sfârșitul lamentabil al mandatului lui Klaus Iohannis / Criticii săi îl numesc "un rege leneș" |url=https://www.g4media.ro/le-figaro-sfarsitul-lamentabil-al-mandatului-lui-klaus-iohannis-criticii-sai-il-numesc-un-rege-lenes.html |access-date=31 December 2024 |website=G4Media.ro |language=ro|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241227111131/https://www.g4media.ro/le-figaro-sfarsitul-lamentabil-al-mandatului-lui-klaus-iohannis-criticii-sai-il-numesc-un-rege-lenes.html|archive-date=27 December 2024|url-status=live}}</ref>

=== President Iohannis' resignation and political crisis ===
Following the annulment of the 2024 presidential election in December, Iohannis was allowed to stay on as president by the [[Constitutional Court of Romania|Constitutional Court]] until his successor could be sworn in. On 10 February, following an attempt by members of parliament to impeach him, Iohannis announced that he would resign on 12 February.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Romania's President Iohannis resigns in face of impeachment threat from hard-right opposition |url=https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20250210-romania-s-outgoing-president-resigns-in-face-of-impeachment-threat-from-opposition |access-date=10 February 2025 |website=France 24|date=10 February 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250210180356/https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20250210-romania-s-outgoing-president-resigns-in-face-of-impeachment-threat-from-opposition |archive-date=10 February 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Senate president [[Ilie Bolojan]] assumed the role of acting president until the elections.<ref>{{Cite web |date=12 February 2025 |title=Romania's Iohannis steps down, leaving caretaker president in charge until election rerun in spring |url=https://apnews.com/article/romania-president-europe-eu-klaus-iohannis-elections-a42440317c1ac55926789f4664656f60 |access-date=12 February 2025 |website=AP News|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250212112811/https://apnews.com/article/romania-president-europe-eu-klaus-iohannis-elections-a42440317c1ac55926789f4664656f60|archive-date=12 February 2025|url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Georgescu barring and Simion candidacy ===
[[File:Georgescu & Simion, BEC 2025 (3).jpg|thumb|[[Călin Georgescu]] (left) arriving to the [[Permanent Electoral Authority (Romania)|Central Electoral Bureau]] to file his candidacy accompanied by his wife Cristela (centre-left) and [[George Simion]] (centre-right). His candidacy was rejected two days later, on March 9, due to legal and procedural issues linked to [[2024 Romanian presidential election|the former presidential elections]] and [[Accusations of Russian interference in the 2024 Romanian presidential election|alleged Russian intervention]] in his favour.]]
On 26 February 2025, Georgescu was stopped by police in traffic, while allegedly on his way to register for the election. He was charged with six offenses, including incitement to actions against the constitutional order, and support of fascist groups.<ref>{{Cite web |date=28 February 2025 |url=https://www.dw.com/en/romania-the-controversy-over-far-right-politician-calin-georgescu/a-71790360 |title=Controversy over far-right Romanian politician Georgescu |access-date=26 February 2025 |website=Deutsche Welle |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250309120605/https://www.dw.com/en/romania-the-controversy-over-far-right-politician-calin-georgescu/a-71790360 |archive-date=9 March 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> Preemptive measures have been imposed, including judiciary control, and a 60-day ban on posting xenophobic and antisemitic materials to social networks (although such actions are already illegal in Romania).<ref name="Georgescu investigation">{{Cite web |date=26 February 2025 |title=Romanian presidential hopeful Călin Georgescu faces criminal investigation|url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/feb/26/romanian-prosecutors-launch-investigation-into-far-right-politician-calin-georgescu |access-date=26 February 2025 |website=The Guardian|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250302015659/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/feb/26/romanian-prosecutors-launch-investigation-into-far-right-politician-calin-georgescu|archive-date=2 March 2025|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=27 February 2025 |title=Georgescu pleaca acasa, insa procurorii au luat mai multe decizii: i-au interzis sa mai apara la televiziuni si in restul presei. Nu are voie nici sa isi faca conturi pe retelele de socializare|url=https://www.aktual24.ro/georgescu-pleaca-acasa-insa-procurorii-au-luat-mai-multe-decizii-i-au-interzis-sa-mai-apara-la-televiziuni-si-in-restul-presei-nu-are-voie-nici-sa-isi-faca-conturi-pe-retelele-de-socializare/ |access-date=26 February 2025 |website=Aktual 24|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250226161413/https://www.aktual24.ro/georgescu-pleaca-acasa-insa-procurorii-au-luat-mai-multe-decizii-i-au-interzis-sa-mai-apara-la-televiziuni-si-in-restul-presei-nu-are-voie-nici-sa-isi-faca-conturi-pe-retelele-de-socializare/|archive-date=26 February 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> The police claimed to have found ten million U.S. dollars buried inside his bodyguard's house along with plane tickets to Moscow.<ref name="Georgescu investigation" /><ref>{{Cite web |date=26 February 2025 |title=Calin Georgescu arrested over $10 million and tickets to Moscow found at his bodyguard's house |url=https://themalteseherald.com/2025/02/26/calin-georgescu-arrested-over-10-million-and-tickets-to-moscow-found-at-his-bodyguards-house/ |access-date=10 March 2025 |website=The Maltese Herald |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250226194824/https://themalteseherald.com/2025/02/26/calin-georgescu-arrested-over-10-million-and-tickets-to-moscow-found-at-his-bodyguards-house/ |archive-date=26 February 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

On 7 March, Georgescu filed his candidacy to the [[Permanent Electoral Authority (Romania)|Central Electoral Bureau]], being rejected two days later which led to new protests.<ref name="Georgescu rejected">{{Cite web |date=9 March 2025 |title=BREAKING Candidatura lui Călin Georgescu, respinsă de Biroul Electoral Central / Violențe în fața BEC, jandarmii au folosit gaze lacrimogene. O parte din protestatari s-au urcat pe ziduri – FOTO, VIDEO |work=HotNews.ro |url=https://hotnews.ro/breaking-candidatura-lui-calin-georgescu-respinsa-de-biroul-electoral-central-manifestantii-din-fata-biroului-electoral-se-imbrancesc-cu-jandarmii-1920222 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250310005149/https://hotnews.ro/breaking-candidatura-lui-calin-georgescu-respinsa-de-biroul-electoral-central-manifestantii-din-fata-biroului-electoral-se-imbrancesc-cu-jandarmii-1920222 |archive-date=10 March 2025 |access-date=9 March 2025 |language=ro}}</ref> Consequently, George Simion arrived to the Central Electoral Bureau on 14 March accompanied by former Polish prime minister [[Mateusz Morawiecki]] to file his candidacy after collecting 604,000 signatures, above the minimum requirement of 200,000.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Otopeanu |first=Cristian |date=15 March 2025 |title=George Simion şi-a depus candidatura la alegerile prezidenţiale 2025 alături de Mateusz Morawiecki, fost premier al Poloniei. Există o contestație pentru Simion |url=https://www.libertatea.ro/stiri/george-simion-depus-candidatura-alegerile-prezidentiale-2025-mateusz-morawiecki-5233114 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250315120311/https://www.libertatea.ro/stiri/george-simion-depus-candidatura-alegerile-prezidentiale-2025-mateusz-morawiecki-5233114 |archive-date=15 March 2025 |access-date=15 March 2025 |work=[[Libertatea]]}}</ref> The CEB approved his candidacy on the following day,<ref>{{Cite press release |title=Comunicat de presă |date=15 March 2025 |publisher=Biroul Electoral Central |url=https://prezidentiale2025.bec.ro/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/CP_23.pdf |access-date=15 March 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250315160230/https://prezidentiale2025.bec.ro/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/CP_23.pdf |archive-date=15 March 2025}}</ref> which was also the deadline for candidates to register, with Simion stating "We passed the BEC, now let's see if we pass the [[Constitutional Court of Romania|CCR]] and return to democracy".<ref>{{Cite news |last=Ion |first=Ioana |date=15 March 2025 |title=Candidatura lui George Simion a fost validată de BEC: "Să vedem dacă trecem de CCR și revenim la democrație" |url=https://www.libertatea.ro/stiri/candidatura-alegeri-prezidentiale-2025-george-simion-validata-de-bec-5233804 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250315154917/https://www.libertatea.ro/stiri/candidatura-alegeri-prezidentiale-2025-george-simion-validata-de-bec-5233804 |archive-date=15 March 2025 |access-date=15 March 2025 |work=Libertatea}}</ref> The CCR validated his candidacy one day later as well as the ones of [[Nicușor Dan]] and [[Victor Ponta]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Petrescu |first=Ana |date=16 March 2025 |title=CCR a respins cele trei contestații privind candidatura lui George Simion. Mesajul președintelui AUR |url=https://www.digi24.ro/stiri/actualitate/politica/ccr-discuta-astazi-13-contestatii-la-mai-multe-candidaturi-printre-care-calin-georgescu-nicusor-dan-victor-ponta-si-george-simion-3159981 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250316192953/https://www.digi24.ro/stiri/actualitate/politica/ccr-discuta-astazi-13-contestatii-la-mai-multe-candidaturi-printre-care-calin-georgescu-nicusor-dan-victor-ponta-si-george-simion-3159981?__grsc=cookieIsUndef0&__grts=58071779&__grua=9e90f00bfd79edbeb2910967839a1fb1&__grrn=1 |archive-date=16 March 2025 |access-date=16 March 2025 |work=[[Digi24]]}}</ref>

== Election date ==
[[File:2025 Romanian presidential election announcement in Belgium.jpg|thumb|Voting locations in Belgium, announcement on [[Tour & Taxis]]]]
The date of the first round had initially been publicly speculated by news media as 23 March 2025, with the runoff two weeks later (6 April 2025). In early January, these dates became obsolete, as the law for electing the [[president of Romania]] requires a minimum of 75 days between the election day and the day the election is called. On 8 January, the coalition fixed the dates of the election. The first round was scheduled to be held on 4 May 2025 with the second round two weeks later (18 May 2025).<ref>{{Cite web |last=Garguli |first=Deniz |date=8 January 2025 |title=Guvernul a decis data noilor alegeri prezidențiale din România. Vor avea loc în luna mai 2025 {{!}} SURSE • Alegeri 2024–2025 |url=https://b365.ro/guvernul-a-decis-data-noilor-alegeri-prezidentiale-din-romania-vor-avea-loc-in-luna-mai-2025-surse-553388/ |access-date=8 January 2025 |website=B365 |language=ro |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250112085418/https://b365.ro/guvernul-a-decis-data-noilor-alegeri-prezidentiale-din-romania-vor-avea-loc-in-luna-mai-2025-surse-553388/|archive-date=12 January 2025|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=8 January 2025 |title=ULTIMA ORĂ DECIZIE Noua dată pentru alegerile prezidențiale. Crin Antonescu rămâne candidat |url=https://www.profit.ro/stiri/politic/ultima-ora-decizie-noua-data-pentru-alegerile-prezidentiale-crin-antonescu-ramane-candidat-21891100 |access-date=8 January 2025 |website=digi24.ro |language=ro |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250119034024/https://www.profit.ro/stiri/politic/ultima-ora-decizie-noua-data-pentru-alegerile-prezidentiale-crin-antonescu-ramane-candidat-21891100 |archive-date=19 January 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-01-16 |title=Romania sets May date for new presidential election |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/1/16/romania-sets-may-date-for-new-presidential-election |access-date=2025-10-26 |website=Al Jazeera |language=en}}</ref>

