== Candidates ==
The Central Electoral Bureau (BEC) was constituted on 21 February 2025.<ref>[https://prezidentiale2025.bec.ro/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/CP_1.pdf BEC 2025 press release] {{Dead link|date=October 2026 |bot=InternetArchiveBot }}</ref> The deadline for registering electoral alliances at the BEC was on 23 February 2025. By that deadline, only one electoral alliance was registered, between the governing [[Social Democratic Party (Romania)|PSD]], [[National Liberal Party (Romania)|PNL]], and [[Democratic Alliance of Hungarians in Romania|UDMR]], called the Romania Forward Electoral Alliance ({{lang|ro|Alianța Electorală România Înainte}}; A.Ro for short).<ref>{{cite web|url=https://prezidentiale2025.bec.ro/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/decizie_1.pdf |title=BEC decision regarding the Romania Forward Alliance A.Ro |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250309121453/https://prezidentiale2025.bec.ro/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/decizie_1.pdf|archive-date=9 March 2025|url-status=live}}</ref>

Persons who wished to run for the office could begin gathering the support signatures (a minimum of 200,000) after 23 February. The deadline for registering the candidacy at the BEC was 15 March 2025, at 23:59:59. All candidatures validated by the BEC had to pass the scrutiny of the [[Constitutional Court of Romania]]. On 19 March, Gavrilă withdrew her candidacy for president, endorsing Simion.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Iana |first=Ciprian |date=20 March 2025 |title=Anamaria Gavrilă a anunțat oficial că se retrage din alegerile prezidențiale 2025: "Am făcut tot ce a depins de mine" |url=https://www.libertatea.ro/stiri/anamaria-gavrila-s-a-retras-din-alegerile-prezidentiale-2025-5239319 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250320081509/https://www.libertatea.ro/stiri/anamaria-gavrila-s-a-retras-din-alegerile-prezidentiale-2025-5239319 |archive-date=20 March 2025 |access-date=20 March 2025 |work=[[Libertatea]]}}</ref> A final list of all 11 candidates was released on the following day.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Arambescu |first=Dana |date=20 March 2025 |title=Lista finală de candidați la alegerile prezidențiale 2025. Cine sunt cei 11 români care vor să ajungă la Cotroceni |url=https://www.libertatea.ro/stiri/lista-finala-candidati-alegeri-prezidentiale-2025-5239359 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250320092245/https://www.libertatea.ro/stiri/lista-finala-candidati-alegeri-prezidentiale-2025-5239359 |archive-date=20 March 2025 |access-date=20 March 2025 |work=[[Libertatea]]}}</ref> On 22 March, a random draw took place, placing Simion on the [[Ballot order effect|first position]] on the ballot and [[Nicușor Dan]] on the last.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Arambescu |first=Dana |date=23 March 2025 |title=Ordinea candidaților pe buletinul de vot la alegerile prezidențiale din 4 mai 2025 |url=https://www.libertatea.ro/stiri/ordinea-candidatilor-buletinul-de-vot-alegerile-prezidentiale-2025-5242788 |work=[[Libertatea]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Specimen ballot paper |url=https://prezidentiale2025.bec.ro/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Specimen_TurI_tara.pdf |website=prezidentiale2025.bec.ro}} {{Dead link|date=October 2026 |bot=InternetArchiveBot }}</ref>

