As per Romanian law, citizens could vote at the designated polling station inside the [[Municipiu|municipality]], [[List of cities and towns in Romania|town]] or [[Communes of Romania|commune]] where they reside or at any other station outside of said jurisdiction, on a supplementary list.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Legea nr. 370/2004 pentru alegerea Preşedintelui României – Art. 44, (4) |trans-title=Law nr. 370/2004 for the election of the President of Romania – Art. 44, (4) |url=https://www.roaep.ro/legislatie/wp-content/uploads/2013/03/Legea-nr.-370-2004-pentru-alegerea-Presedintelui-Romaniei-1.pdf |website=Autoritatea Electorală Permanentă (Permanent Electoral Authority) |language=ro}}</ref> The counting process was recorded.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Coșlea |first=Alexandra |date=17 May 2025 |title=Alegeri prezidențiale 2025, turul 2. BEC lămurește cum se vor numără voturile în secții |trans-title=2025 presidential elections, round 2. BEC clarifies how votes will be counted in polling stations |url=https://hotnews.ro/alegeri-prezidentiale-2025-turul-2-bec-lamureste-cum-se-vor-numara-voturile-in-sectii-1978231 |work=HotNews |language=ro}}</ref> Fifty-three Romanian politically non-affiliated organisations were accredited by the [[Permanent Electoral Authority (Romania)|Permanent Electoral Authority]] to observe the election process.<ref>{{Cite web |date=18 May 2025 |title=Comunicat de presă privind regulile pe care trebuie să le respecte observatorii interni desemnați de către asociații și fundații să observe procesul electoral din 18 mai 2025 |trans-title=Press release on the rules that must be respected by domestic observers appointed by associations and foundations to observe the electoral process of May 18, 2025 |url=https://www.roaep.ro/prezentare/comunicat-de-presa/comunicat-de-presa-privind-regulile-pe-care-trebuie-sa-le-respecte-observatorii-interni-desemnati-de-catre-asociatii-si-fundatii-sa-observe-procesul-electoral-din-18-mai-2025/ |website=Autoritatea Electorală Permanentă (Permanent Electoral Authority) |language=ro}}</ref> The [[Permanent Electoral Authority (Romania)|AEP]] additionally approved access for 87 foreign journalists from outlets such as [[Sky News]], [[Associated Press]], [[Reuters]], [[France 24]] and the [[BBC News|BBC]] as well as 159 representatives of the following organisations:<ref>{{Cite news |date=18 May 2025 |title=AEP a acreditat 87 de jurnalişti străini şi 159 de observatori internaţionali pentru turul doi al alegerilor prezidențiale 2025 |trans-title=AEP accredited 87 foreign journalists and 159 international observers for the second round of the 2025 presidential elections |url=https://www.g4media.ro/aep-a-acreditat-87-de-jurnalisti-straini-si-159-de-observatori-internationali-pentru-turul-doi-al-alegerilor-prezidentiale-2025.html |work=G4Media |language=ro}}</ref>
