Results were updated in real time on the Permanent Electoral Authority website with information from the 19,943 polling stations.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Bercea |first=Alexandra |date=18 May 2025 |title=Unde poți urmări, în timp real, prezența și rezultatele turului 2 al alegerilor prezidențiale din 2025 |trans-title=Where can you follow, in real time, the turnout and results of the 2nd round of the 2025 presidential elections |url=https://www.libertatea.ro/stiri/prezenta-rezultate-tur-2-alegeri-prezidentiale-2025-5310872 |work=Libertatea |language=ro}}</ref> There were no major incidents reported by observers during voting hours or the counting process.<ref>{{Cite news |date=5 May 2025 |title=AEP: Observatorii internaţionali au afirmat că alegerile s-au desfăşurat într-un climat de corectitudine, integritate şi transparenţă |trans-title=AEP: International observers stated that the elections were conducted in a climate of fairness, integrity and transparency. |url=https://www.g4media.ro/aep-observatorii-internationali-au-afirmat-ca-alegerile-s-au-desfasurat-intr-un-climat-de-corectitudine-integritate-si-transparenta.html |work=G4Media |language=ro}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Eduard |first=Sebastian |date=19 May 2025 |title=MAI: Alegerile prezidenţiale, fără incidente deosebite. Care a fost problema cea mai des semnalată |trans-title=MAI: Presidential elections, without any major incidents. What was the most frequently reported problem |url=https://www.digi24.ro/alegeri-prezidentiale-2025/mai-alegerile-prezidentiale-fara-incidente-deosebite-care-a-fost-problema-cea-mai-des-semnalata-3247069 |work=Digi24 |language=ro}}</ref> Statements of preliminary conclusions from the [[Parliamentary Assembly of the Organization for Security and Co-operation in Europe|Parliamentary Assembly of the OSCE]] mention that "[t]he voting process was evaluated positively, with observers finding the process to be conducted in an efficient, transparent, and professional manner", while also noting the presence of online [[disinformation]] and [[media bias]] during the campaign.<ref>{{Cite web |date=18 May 2025 |title=INTERNATIONAL ELECTION OBSERVATION MISSION Romania – Presidential Election, Second Round |url=https://www.osce.org/files/f/documents/d/8/590963.pdf |website=OSCE PA}}</ref> [[Federal Election Commission|FEC]] member [[James E. Trainor III|Trey Trainor]] praised the election process he observed, stating that: "Every vote was cast using a paper ballot, and the entire ballot-counting process was not only done in the presence of poll watchers from every political party but also recorded on video to guarantee transparency. There were no delays in reporting results. In fact, the entire country completed its electoral count within hours of polls closing — a testament to both the simplicity and the integrity of the process."<ref>{{Cite news |last=Trainor |first=Trey |date=9 May 2025 |title=What Romania can teach America about election integrity |url=https://www.washingtonexaminer.com/opinion/3405115/romania-us-election-integrity/ |work=Washington Examiner}}</ref>

