==Aftermath==

===First round===
[[File:George Simion cu media 4.5.2025 (7).jpg|thumb|Simion at a press conference on 4 May with [[Silvia Uscov]], [[Petrișor Peiu]] and [[Ryszard Czarnecki]] ]]
Following the results, Prime Minister [[Marcel Ciolacu]] announced that PSD would leave [[Romania Forward Electoral Alliance|A.Ro]], and he resigned from the position of prime minister, which resulted in the collapse of the coalition. However, he continued to serve as the PSD leader.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Marcel Ciolacu: PSD a votat în unanimitate ieşirea de la guvernare, prin urmare demisia mea, şi că nu va susţine niciun candidat în turul 2 |url=https://observatornews.ro/politic/surse-marcel-ciolacu-siar-putea-da-demisia-de-la-sefia-psd-dupa-esecul-lui-crin-antonescu-la-prezidentiale-618483.html |access-date=5 May 2025 |website=Observator News |language=RO}}</ref> Lasconi got significantly fewer votes than in the 2024 elections, scoring only 2.68% of the vote.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Reprezentare grafică |url=https://prezenta.roaep.ro/prezidentiale04052025/pv/romania/results/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250505093832/https://prezenta.roaep.ro/prezidentiale04052025/pv/romania/results/ |archive-date=5 May 2025 |access-date=5 May 2025 |website=prezenta.roaep.ro}}</ref> Subsequently, the next day after the elections, she announced she would step down as president of the Save Romania Union.<ref>{{Cite web |date=5 May 2025 |title=Elena Lasconi demisionează de la conducerea USR |url=https://www.digi24.ro/stiri/actualitate/politica/elena-lasconi-demisioneaza-de-la-conducerea-usr-3226997 |access-date=5 May 2025 |website=Digi24|language=ro}}</ref> Simion's victory in the first round also had significant economic implications, with the [[Bucharest Stock Exchange]] experiencing substantial losses,<ref>{{Cite web |title=Bursa e în scădere după ce George Simion a câștigat primul tur al alegerilor prezidențiale. Toți indicii sunt pe roșu |url=https://stirileprotv.ro/stiri/financiar/bursa-de-valori-bucuresti-reactioneaza-negativ-dupa-primul-tur-de-alegeri-toti-indicii-sunt-in-scadere.html |access-date=6 May 2025 |website=Știrile ProTV |language=ro}}</ref> and the [[National Bank of Romania]] investing over 2 billion euros in stabilising the leu and preventing depreciation.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Pantazi |first=Cristian |date=6 May 2025 |title=EXCLUSIV: BNR a cheltuit 2 miliarde de euro într-o singură zi ca să mențină cursul stabil al leului după victoria lui George Simion în turul 1. BNR: "În ultima perioadă a apărut o schimbare importantă pe piața valutară" |url=https://www.g4media.ro/banca-nationala-a-cheltuit-2-miliarde-de-euro-intr-o-singura-zi-ca-sa-mentina-cursul-stabil-al-leului-dupa-victoria-lui-george-simion-in-turul-1-surse.html |access-date=6 May 2025 |website=G4Media.ro |language=ro-RO}}</ref>

Former Romanian president [[Traian Băsescu]] criticised the [[Romanian diaspora]] for Simion's victory among its voters. He called the attitude of the majority of the diaspora "dishonest", stating that: "They live in the West and say: come on, you who live at home, come on, go to daddy Putin, go to Putin!".<ref>{{cite news |date=5 May 2025 |title=Băsescu critică dur diaspora: "Ei trăiesc în Occident și spun: voi care trăiți acasă, ia treceți către tătucu' Putin" |url=https://stirileprotv.ro/alegeri/prezidentiale/2024/basescu-critica-dur-diaspora-zei-traiesc-in-occident-si-spun-voi-care-traiti-acasa-ia-treceti-catre-tatucu-putin.html |publisher=Pro TV |language=ro}}</ref> During the campaign, AUR appointed lawyer [[Silvia Uscov]] head of its legal team to help in possibly challenging the election results.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Velasco |first=Sergio |date=26 May 2025 |title=Silvia Uscov, abogada del equipo jurídico de George Simion: «Las instituciones diplomáticas fueron utilizadas con fines partidistas» |url=https://gaceta.es/entrevista/silvia-uscov-abogada-del-equipo-juridico-de-george-simion-las-instituciones-diplomaticas-fueron-utilizadas-con-fines-partidistas-20250526-0025/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250526031010/https://gaceta.es/entrevista/silvia-uscov-abogada-del-equipo-juridico-de-george-simion-las-instituciones-diplomaticas-fueron-utilizadas-con-fines-partidistas-20250526-0025/ |archive-date=26 May 2025 |access-date=30 May 2025 |work=[[La Gaceta (Spain)|La Gaceta]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Uscov |first=Silvia |date=17 June 2025 |title=Exclusive: Lawyer behind George Simion tells us what really happened in presidential campaign |url=https://brusselssignal.eu/2025/06/exclusive-the-lawyer-behind-george-simion-tells-us-what-really-happened-in-presidential-campaign/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250820113907/https://brusselssignal.eu/2025/06/exclusive-the-lawyer-behind-george-simion-tells-us-what-really-happened-in-presidential-campaign/ |archive-date=20 August 2025 |access-date=7 July 2025 |work=Brussels Signal}}</ref> Simion was congratulated on his first-round win by [[Mateusz Morawiecki]], former Polish prime minister and current president of the [[European Conservatives and Reformists Party|European Conservatives and Reformists]], Italy's Deputy Prime Minister [[Matteo Salvini]] and French MEP [[Marion Maréchal]].<ref name="Right-wing jubilation" />

==== Analysis ====
After Simion's first-round victory, Moldovan analyst Ion Tăbîrță predicted that, if Simion were to prevail in the second round, [[Moldova-Romania relations]] would suffer. Tăbîrță claimed that, were Simion to win, Moldova could lose Romania's support in international relations, including in its path toward [[European integration]]. He added that Romania would lose its role as Moldova's "defender" in the eyes of the European Union, as it would no longer have the same image within the bloc. According to another Moldovan analyst, Mihaela Sirețanu, relations between the two countries would become tense: Simion is banned from entering Moldova until 2028. Both Tăbîrță and Sirețanu agreed that Dan's victory would be more favourable for Moldova and its relationship with Romania.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://adevarul.ro/stiri-externe/republica-moldova/george-simion-vs-nicusor-dan-la-cotroceni-cine-2441074.html|title=George Simion vs. Nicușor Dan la Cotroceni: Cine ar conta mai mult pentru Republica Moldova ANALIZĂ|first=Alina|last=Cotoros|newspaper=Adevărul|date=6 May 2025|language=ro}}</ref> BBC's Central Europe Correspondent [[Nick Thorpe]] reported that many voters who backed Georgescu in the annulled election switched their allegiance to Simion, and that the two voted together. He predicted that, in the second round, Simion would also attract voters who backed fourth-placed former Prime Minister Victor Ponta, a retired Social Democrat who adopted a "Romania First" campaign.<ref>{{Cite web |date=5 May 2025 |title=Nationalist Simion wins first round of Romanian election rerun |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cj0zl1702ego |access-date=8 May 2025 |website=BBC |language=en-GB}}</ref>

===Second round===
[[File:Romanian Presidential Elections 2025 - Results.svg|thumb|400px|Results of the presidential election]]
[[File:Romanian diaspora votes by European countries in Romania 2025 elections.svg|thumb|300x300px|First place diaspora votes in Europe by country:{{Legend|#33A02C|Nicușor Dan}}{{Legend|#FF7F00|George Simion}}]]
On the day of the second round, Andrei Țărnea, spokesman of the [[Ministry of Foreign Affairs (Romania)|Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Romania]], denounced Russian interference during the election. He stated that a viral [[fake news]] campaign on [[Telegram (software)|Telegram]] and other social media was seeking to influence the electoral process, something which was expected as he stated, with the Romanian authorities having proved these news false according to him. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs stated this situation was alarming because "it appears to have been created with the aim of undermining citizens' confidence in democratic institutions and processes". Furthermore, the [[Ministry of Internal Affairs (Romania)|Ministry of Internal Affairs of Romania]] stated that a clip had been distributed on TikTok claiming that [[Mission Aigle|French troops in Romania]], stationed at [[NATO]]'s [[Cincu Training Center]], were secretly wearing [[Gendarmerie (Romania)|Romanian Gendarmerie]] uniforms to intervene on Romania's internal affairs, which the ministry stated was false and "pure disinformation".<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.euronews.ro/articole/mae-denunta-o-interferenta-ruseasca-in-timpul-alegerilor-prezidentiale-din-romani|title=MAE denunță o "interferență rusească" în timpul alegerilor prezidențiale din România. "Încă o dată vedem semnele distinctive"|publisher=Euronews România|date=18 May 2025|language=ro}}</ref>

With a final voter turnout of 64.72% (which translates to 11,641,544 votes),<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://prezenta.roaep.ro/prezidentiale18052025/presence/table/?region=total|title=Presidential Elections – Round 2 (Voting Presence data)}}</ref> the run-off winner was certified on 18 May by the Central Electoral Bureau to be Dan, with 6,168,642 votes.<ref>{{Cite web |date=18 May 2025 |title=Proces verbal privind rezultatul alegerilor pentru Președintele României în cadrul celui de-al doilea tur de scrutin – 18 mai 2025|trans-title=Minutes of the second round of elections for the President of Romania – May 18, 2025 |url=https://prezidentiale2025.bec.ro/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/RFT1_2.pdf |access-date=20 May 2025}}</ref> Simion had prematurely declared victory on [[Facebook]] with a post reading: "I won!!! I am the new President of Romania and I am giving back the power to the Romanians!"<ref>{{Cite web |date=18 May 2025 |title=Romania: Pro-Russian Simion claims victory in elections, but pro-European Dan actually wins |url=https://news.liga.net/en/politics/news/romania-pro-russian-simion-claims-victory-in-elections-but-pro-european-dan-actually-wins |access-date=19 May 2025 |website=LIGA |language=en}}</ref> He later conceded the election, stating "I would like to congratulate my opponent, Nicușor Dan. He won the election, it was the will of the Romanian people".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Ilie |first1=Luiza |last2=Gladun |first2=Elizaveta |title=Centrist Dan wins Romanian presidency over hard-right pro-Trump rival |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/europe/romanians-vote-presidential-run-off-that-could-widen-eu-rifts-2025-05-17/ |website=[[Reuters]] |date=19 May 2025 |access-date=19 May 2025}}</ref><ref name=":6">{{Cite news |date=19 May 2025 |title=George Simion recunoaşte că a pierdut alegerile: Am fost singuri împotriva tuturor |trans-title=George Simion admits he lost the elections: We were alone against everyone |url=https://observatornews.ro/alegeri-prezidentiale-2024/george-simion-recunoaste-ca-a-pierdut-alegerile-am-fost-singuri-impotriva-tuturor-619820.html |work=Observator |language=ro}}</ref> Two days later, Simion demanded the annulment of the election, citing "external influence by state and non-state actors" as grounds for annulment, drawing parallels to the court's previous annulment of the December 2024 election over alleged Russian interference, referring to the election as a "farce".<ref>{{cite tweet |user=georgesimion |number=1924859475573305748 |title=I officially ask Constitutional Court TO ANNUL Romanian presidential elections |date=20 May 2025 |access-date=21 May 2025}}</ref>

Telegram founder Pavel Durov claimed meanwhile on May 18 that he had been pressured in France in the spring of 2025 to have Telegram remove certain "conservative" messages during the May 2025 presidential election.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-05-18 |title=Présidentielle en Roumanie: le patron de Telegram accuse la France d'"ingérence", Paris dénonce des allégations "infondées" |url=https://www.bfmtv.com/international/europe/presidentielle-en-roumanie-le-patron-de-telegram-accuse-la-france-d-ingerence-paris-denonce-des-allegations-infondees_AN-202505180359.html |access-date=2025-07-11 |website=BFMTV |language=fr}}</ref><ref name=":7">{{Cite news |date=2025-05-18 |title=Telegram founder says he rejected a Western request to silence conservative voices in Romania |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/europe/telegram-founder-says-he-rejects-request-silence-conservative-voices-romania-2025-05-18/ |access-date=2025-07-11 |work=Reuters |language=en}}</ref> The Ministry of Foreign Affairs in France formally denied this in a statement.<ref name=":5" /> Following this denial, Durov specifically accused [[Nicolas Lerner]], [[Directorate General for External Security|Director General of External Security]] (DGSE), of having asked him to carry out this censorship.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-06-19 |title=EXCLUSIVE. Pavel Durov on his arrest in France, Macron, Russia, the FBI — and the fight for Telegram |url=https://www.lepoint.fr/high-tech-internet/exclusive-pavel-durov-on-his-arrest-in-france-macron-russia-the-fbi-and-the-fight-for-telegram-19-06-2025-2592412_47.php |access-date=2025-07-11 |website=Le Point |language=fr}}</ref> He did not provide any proof for either of these accusations.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Leloup |first=Damien |date=2025-05-22 |title=Roumanie : à quoi joue Pavel Durov, le fondateur de Telegram qui accuse la France d'ingérence ? |url=https://www.lemonde.fr/pixels/article/2025/05/22/accusations-d-ingerence-a-quoi-joue-pavel-durov_6607799_4408996.html |access-date=2025-07-19 |work=[[Le Monde]] |language=fr}}</ref>

On 21 May, seven out of the 21 [[Chamber of Deputies (Romania)|deputies]] and five out of the seven [[Senate of Romania|senators]] of the right-wing populist [[Party of Young People]] left the party, bringing the parliamentary group in the [[Senate of Romania|Senate]] below the minimum threshold of members and causing its dissolution.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Petrescu |first=Ana |date=21 May 2025 |title=POT a pierdut o treime dintre deputați. Gavrilă: "I-au trădat pe români. Partidul Oamenilor Tineri nu e o umbrelă pentru carieriști" |trans-title=POT lost a third of its deputies. Gavrilă: "They betrayed Romanians. The Party of Young People is not an umbrella for careerists" |url=https://www.digi24.ro/stiri/actualitate/politica/pot-a-pierdut-o-treime-dintre-deputati-gavrila-i-au-tradat-pe-romani-partidul-oamenilor-tineri-nu-e-o-umbrela-pentru-carieristi-3250097 |work=Digi24 |language=ro}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Hoară |first=Robert |date=21 May 2025 |title=Cu doar doi senatori, grupul parlamentar POT din Senat va fi dizolvat automat după demisiile numeroase |trans-title=With only two senators, the POT parliamentary group in the Senate will be automatically dissolved after numerous resignations |url=https://stirileprotv.ro/stiri/politic/cu-doar-2-senatori-grupul-parlamentar-pot-din-senat-va-fi-dizolvat-automat-dupa-demisiile-numeroase.html |work=PRO TV |language=ro}}</ref> On May 22, the Constitutional Court rejected Simion's request and upheld the initial results, thus validating Dan's election.<ref name=":9">{{Cite web |last=Ion |first=Ioana |date=2025-05-22 |title=CCR a validat rezultatele alegerilor prezidențiale. Cererea de anulare, depusă de George Simion, a fost respinsă |url=https://www.libertatea.ro/stiri/ccr-valideaza-rezultatele-alegerilor-prezidentiale-nicusor-dan-presedinte-5317369 |access-date=2025-05-22 |website=Libertatea |language=ro}}</ref> Dan was sworn in on 26 May in front of the Romanian Parliament.<ref>{{Cite web |date=26 May 2025 |title=Discursul susținut de Președintele României, Nicușor Dan, în cadrul ședinței solemne comune a Camerei Deputaților și a Senatului, consacrată depunerii jurământului de învestitură în funcție |url=https://www.presidency.ro/ro/presedinte/agenda-presedintelui/discursul-sustinut-de-presedintele-romaniei-nicusor-dan-in-cadrul-sedintei-solemne-comune-a-camerei-deputatilor-si-a-senatului-consacrata-depunerii-juramantului-de-investitura-in-functie1748254523}}</ref> In a statement published on 26 May 2025, the AUR party claimed that Lerner had "discreetly" traveled to Romania before the second round of elections.<ref name=":10">{{Cite web |title=SIE:French foreign intelligence service head did not visit Romania; attempts at manipulation and disinformation - AGERPRES |url=https://agerpres.ro/english/2025/05/30/sie-french-foreign-intelligence-service-head-did-not-visit-romania-attempts-at-manipulation-and-disi--1454664 |access-date=2025-07-11 |website=agerpres.ro}}</ref> These [[fake news]] were denied by the Romanian Foreign Intelligence Service,<ref name=":13">{{Cite web |last=Gubert |first=Romain |date=2025-06-18 |title=Ce que la DGSE répond à Pavel Durov |url=https://www.lepoint.fr/monde/la-dgse-repond-a-pavel-durov-ca-ressemble-a-une-manipulation-des-services-russes-18-06-2025-2592401_24.php |access-date=2025-07-19 |website=Le Point |language=fr}}</ref> calling them "attempts at manipulation and disinformation",<ref name=":6" /> and by French DGSE.<ref name=":7" />

==== International reactions ====
Several leaders from across Europe congratulated Dan on his election; they included French president [[Emmanuel Macron]], Ukrainian president [[Volodymyr Zelenskyy]], Moldovan president [[Maia Sandu]], Polish prime minister [[Donald Tusk]], and European Commission president [[Ursula von der Leyen]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-05-19 |title=Nicușor Dan, felicitat de Ursula von der Leyen, Emmanuel Macron și Volodimir Zelenski, după victoria în alegeri |url=https://stirileprotv.ro/alegeri/prezidentiale/2024/ursula-von-der-leyen-dupa-victoria-lui-nicusor-dan-romanii-au-ales-promisiunea-unei-tari-prospere-intr-o-europa-puternica.html |access-date=2025-05-25 |website=Știrile ProTV |language=ro}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-05-19 |title=Liderii lumii îl felicită pe Nicușor Dan pentru victoria în alegeri |url=https://www.digi24.ro/alegeri-prezidentiale-2025/liderii-lumii-il-felicita-pe-nicusor-dan-pentru-victoria-in-alegeri-3246685?__grsc=cookieIsUndef0&__grts=58273549&__grua=eb350cc589d58cb5ada88eadfb38fadf&__grrn=1 |access-date=2025-05-25 |website=Digi24 |language=ro}}</ref> Russian presidential spokesperson [[Dmitry Peskov]] called the election results "strange, to say the least", and said Dan had won "in the absence of the favorite", referring to Georgescu.<ref>{{Cite web |date=19 May 2025 |title=Kremlin Calls Romanian Presidential Election 'Strange' After Centrist Defeats Far-Right Rival |url=https://www.themoscowtimes.com/2025/05/19/kremlin-calls-romanian-presidential-election-strange-after-centrist-defeats-far-right-rival-a89125 |access-date=20 May 2025 |website=The Moscow Times |language=en}}</ref> The French intelligence agency [[DGSE]] denied claims by George Simion and [[Telegram (software)|Telegram]] founder [[Pavel Durov]] that it had interfered with the election.<ref>{{Cite web |date=19 May 2025 |title=France 'strongly refutes' Telegram founder's allegations of meddling in Romanian elections |url=https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20250519-france-strongly-refutes-telegram-founder-s-allegations-of-meddling-in-romanian-elections |access-date=20 May 2025 |website=France 24 |language=en}}</ref>

==== Institutions ====
[[File:Roberta Metsola, EP President meets with Nicușor Dan, President-Elect of Romania.jpg|thumb|European Parliament President [[Roberta Metsola]] visiting Romania and meeting with President Dan|250px]]

* {{flag|European Union}}: President of the European Parliament [[Roberta Metsola]] spoke with Dan to congratulate him on his election. She noted that after the announcement of the results, it was deeply moving to see EU flags waved across Romania. Metsola emphasized that the Romanian people could trust and rely on Europe, and she announced that she would visit Romania later that week to deliver this message.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://x.com/EP_President/status/1924422145586643259 |title= Great speaking with @NicusorDanRO to congratulate him on his election as President of Romania.|publisher=Roberta Metsola |date=18 May 2025 |access-date=18 May 2025}}</ref>
* {{flag|NATO}}: Secretary General of NATO [[Mark Rutte]] congratulated Dan in a phone call, stressing that both sides shared the important responsibility of ensuring collective security. He underlined that a strong NATO would promote regional stability and expressed his expectation of close cooperation with Dan, particularly at the upcoming [[NATO Summit]] in [[The Hague]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://x.com/SecGenNATO/status/1924418022346793361 |title= Just had a call with @NicusorDanRO to congratulate him on his election win.|publisher=Mark Rutte |date=18 May 2025 |access-date=18 May 2025}}</ref>

==== Analysis ====
Dan's victory in the second round was unexpected,<ref>{{Cite web |title=Pro-EU moderate Nicușor Dan wins Romanian presidential election stunner |url=https://www.politico.eu/article/romanian-presidential-election-results-nicusor-dan-george-simion/|access-date=26 May 2025 |website=Politico|date=18 May 2025 |language=en}}</ref><ref name=dan-simion-le-monde/> and analysts attributed it to higher voter turnout.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Centrist Nicuşor Dan defeats far-right rival in Romanian presidential election |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/may/18/centrist-nicusor-dan-on-course-to-beat-far-right-rival-in-romanian-election-exit-polls-suggest|access-date=26 May 2025 |website=The Guardian|date=18 May 2025 |language=en |last1=Henley |first1=Jon }}</ref> [[Urban–rural political divide|Urban voters]], women, and ethnic minorities voted for Dan over Simion by large margins.<ref name=dan-simion-le-monde>{{Cite web |title=Romanian election: How pro-European candidate Nicusor Dan won a surprise victory|url=https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2025/05/21/romanian-election-how-pro-european-candidate-nicusor-dan-won-a-surprise-victory_6741495_4.html|access-date=26 May 2025 |website=Le Monde|date=21 May 2025 |language=en}}</ref> Dan did particularly well among Romania's large population of [[Hungarians in Romania|ethnic Hungarians]], who were wary of Simion's nationalist rhetoric despite Hungarian prime minister [[Viktor Orbán]]'s apparent endorsement of Simion in the second round. Orbán's endorsement was poorly received in both [[Hungary]] and the diaspora.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Blackburn |first1=Gavin |last2=Tanács |first2=Gábor |date=21 May 2025 |title=Hungarian minority plays key role in Nicușor Dan's Romanian presidential win |url=https://www.euronews.com/2025/05/21/hungarian-minority-plays-key-role-in-nicusor-dans-romanian-presidential-win |access-date=5 July 2025 |work=Euro News}}</ref> ''[[The New York Times]]'' columnist Andrew Higgins also opined that Dan's victory indicated that voters "wanted a middle path between bitterly polarized political camps,"<ref>{{Cite web |title=In Upset, Centrist Wins Romania's Presidential Election |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/05/18/world/europe/nicusor-dan-romania-election.html|access-date=26 May 2025 |website=The New York Times|date=18 May 2025 |language=en |last1=Higgins |first1=Andrew }}</ref> while the ''[[Atlantic Council]]'' argued that Dan benefited from not being associated with the ruling government, and that "Romanians have voted for Europe and democracy, not nationalism, but they also seem to want change."<ref>{{Cite web |title=Experts react: What message did Romanians send by electing Nicusor Dan?|url=https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/new-atlanticist/experts-react/what-message-did-romanians-send-by-electing-nicusor-dan/|access-date=26 May 2025 |website=Atlantic Council|date=19 May 2025 |language=en}}</ref> Political analyst and AUR senate leader [[Petrișor Peiu]] attributed the result to Dan's strong [[Mass mobilization|mobilisation efforts]] as well as "less inspired" decisions by AUR.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Georgescu |first=Andrei |date=19 May 2025 |title=Cauzele înfrângerii lui George Simion în alegeri, explicate de un lider AUR: Unele decizii care s-au luat la noi, mai puțin inspirate |url=https://hotnews.ro/cauzele-infrangerii-lui-george-simion-in-alegeri-explicate-de-un-lider-aur-unele-decizii-care-s-au-luat-la-noi-mai-putin-inspirate-1980577 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250519123441/https://hotnews.ro/cauzele-infrangerii-lui-george-simion-in-alegeri-explicate-de-un-lider-aur-unele-decizii-care-s-au-luat-la-noi-mai-putin-inspirate-1980577 |archive-date=19 May 2025 |access-date=19 May 2025 |work=[[HotNews]]}}</ref>

